<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101416" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συσσί̄τ-ιον</span></b> , τό, only
		in pl. (exc. in <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ion</u>
			1165
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>common meal, public
				mess</i>, such as were used in Crete and Sparta, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				715
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				625e
			</span></i>, etc.; cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1271a33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1272a1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1330a3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>mess, company</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxil.
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>mess-room, common-hall</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν μέσῳ συσσιτίῳ κρατῆρας ἔστησ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συσσίτια ἐν οἷς . . τὴν δίαιταν
					ποιητέον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					762c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. χειμερινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Criti.</u>
					112b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυμνάσια ς. τε</span> ibid.c;
				<i>common-room</i> of the Museum at Alexandria, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.1.8
			</span></i>.</div>
